# Which duplicate rule wins depends on ananicy-cpp's directory walk, not on file names: on the MSI (2026-11-03) the same file as zz-agents.rules was ignored and as 00-0-agents.rules it works (the LENOVO's zz-* works). After a reinstall, msi-tuning-check proves it with a node probe.
# Local override (nadavcohen, 2026-11-03): agent builds/tests/MCP servers run under node/bun/rsync.
# CachyOS default puts them in BG_CPUIO (SCHED_IDLE + idle I/O), which starves them behind anything else.
# Same level as the agent-nice convention (nice 10, best-effort I/O). Rollback: delete this file, restart ananicy-cpp.
{ "name": "node", "nice": 10, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 5 }
{ "name": "MainThread", "nice": 10, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 5 }
{ "name": "bun", "nice": 10, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 5 }
{ "name": "rsync", "nice": 10, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 6 }
# MSI (2026-11-03): the MSI is driven over ssh from the LENOVO; CachyOS puts sshd/sshd-session in BG_CPUIO,
# so every remote command inherits SCHED_IDLE and starves behind any normal load. Normal priority instead.
{ "name": "sshd", "nice": 0, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 4 }
{ "name": "sshd-session", "nice": 0, "sched": "other", "ioclass": "best-effort", "ionice": 4 }
